24:     Expand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.
25: 
26:     Input structure
27:     The input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.
28:     The legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,
29:     the same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.
30: 
31:     Rule
32:     Pair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in
33:     the lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,
34:     recoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.
35: 
36:     Key insight
37:     The lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select
38:     the stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.
