280:     - A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.
281: 
282:     Rule:
283:     - Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.
284:     - Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.
285:     - For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.
286: 
287:     Key insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.
